Third-party software in the PDF toolchain
-----------------------------------------
pdfplumber depends on pypdfium2, whose wheels bundle the PDFium library and its
third-party components (the PDF toolchain is not used for rendering by this product).
Portions of this software are copyright (c) The FreeType Project (www.freetype.org).
All rights reserved. FreeType is used under the FreeType Project License (FTL):
https://freetype.org/license.html
This software is based in part on the work of the Independent JPEG Group (IJG);
the bundled libjpeg-turbo is licensed under the IJG licence and the BSD 3-clause
licence: https://github.com/libjpeg-turbo/libjpeg-turbo/blob/main/LICENSE.md
Other bundled components carry permissive licences (libpng, BSD, MIT, Apache-2.0, ISC,
Zlib, Unicode); see the notices shipped inside the pypdfium2 wheel.
Only glibc (manylinux), macOS and Windows wheels are supported. CI runs on Ubuntu (glibc);
there is no backend Docker image. A test checks the installed pypdfium2 wheel tag.
